IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- LAYER 1, MODULE 7: REGULATION 4 (the Table
-- of revocations), as DATA.
--
-- Regulation 4 revokes thirteen earlier instruments, wholly or in part. That is an act
-- done to OTHER instruments, and it gives the person nothing to ask (reg 3 is where
-- the person feels it: "despite the revocation ... the greater amount shall be
-- payable"). It is encoded as a Table so that reg 3(1)'s "(a) ... (b)" can be shown to
-- be two of the rows revoked in whole, and so that nothing in the text is left
-- unaccounted for. The seat layer has no question on it.
--
-- THE CONVERTER FUSED THE FOOTNOTE NUMBER TO THE YEAR: "Regulations 19761" is the
-- year 1976 followed by footnote 1, and "Regulations (Northern Ireland) 199810" is
-- 1998 followed by footnote 10. The quotation below is the converter's text, as it
-- must be; the `instrument` strings are the same words with the footnote number
-- removed, and each `citation` is the footnote text without its number (src:61-73).
-- The row number is the footnote number, and each citation's S.I. or S.R. number
-- agrees with the year in the title on every row (checked by eye, row by row).
--
-- Ruler of the rows below:
--   row, instrument, citation, extent of revocation

§ `Regulation 4: revocations`

